# TypeScript & tsconfig

Align new and edited code with `tsconfig.json` (strict mode, `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters`, `noFallthroughCasesInSwitch`).

- Prefer `import type` for imports that are only used as types.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — type-only import
import type { Look } from '../types';
import { useState } from 'react';

// ❌ AVOID — value import used only as a type
import { Look } from '../types';
```

- Do not relax compiler options in one-off files; fix types or narrow unions instead.

- Keep TypeScript source files on `.ts`. This repo does not use `.tsx`; React views should use `createElement` when they need to stay in TypeScript.
